"""Speaker notes. Each says what is live today, what is proposed or vision, what is proven, and the sources."""

N1 = """About 20 seconds.
Say: This is a proposal, not a product announcement. Many people already have an agent. The headline is the main idea: Tsenta's job search as a layer inside the agent you already use. Anyone with an agent has two choices: connect Tsenta to it, or switch to Tsenta's own agent. Anyone without one gets Tsenta's agent, starting with the job. Keeping the job and the rest of life are the vision, so nobody is turned away. Only the job agent and its doors are live today.
Point at the legend: every slide is marked LIVE TODAY (Tsenta's public job agent), PROPOSED (designed, not built), VISION (not built, demand not proven) or SYNTHETIC (made-up data).
Live today: Tsenta's job agent and its doors (slide 4). Proposed: the shared core, approvals and pilot. Vision: everything about life. Proven: nothing beyond the public product.
Headline: the owner's reframe of Oct 14 (existing-agent add-on first, the switch option explicit). Earlier headline "Starts with your job. Grows into your life." retired.
Do not say: another agent behaves exactly like Tsenta's own (parity is being researched, not claimed); that ChatGPT, Muse or any host not on tsenta.com/mcp works with Tsenta today; that nobody else offers job tools over MCP (not checked); that any ChatGPT user can add Tsenta (full use is Business, Enterprise and Edu, admin-enabled, web only; Pro is read-only); that Muse or Instinct support MCP; that Tsenta imports memory or chat history; that Tsenta is proactive inside other agents; any proven auth flaw."""

N2 = """About 40 seconds. LIVE TODAY, all public, read at source on Oct 13.
Say: You already have both paths' doors: an MCP server inside people's AI for the connect path, and texting on iMessage and WhatsApp plus the apps for Tsenta's own agent. So this pitch is not "add a channel". It proposes one brain behind the doors. Public docs do not show one today; we do not know what exists internally, so do not say it is missing.
Quotes:
- tsenta.com: "Text Tsenta the roles you want. Reply yes to a match; the application happens in the background and you get the receipt." Also "submits a tailored resume the moment a fitting role goes up". https://tsenta.com/
- tsenta.com/messaging: "Text to Apply or via WhatsApp". https://tsenta.com/messaging
- tsenta.com/mcp: "Run your job search from inside your AI"; clients listed: Claude Code, Claude Desktop & Web, Cursor, Codex CLI. https://tsenta.com/mcp
- docs.tsenta.com: "Approval behavior depends on your client; connecting it does not guarantee it will prompt before every change." https://docs.tsenta.com/product/mcp-connector (re-read 2026-10-14 01:41 CDT as .md and as the rendered page; the sentence is present in both)
The right-hand panel is our proposal, not a criticism of what ships."""

N3 = """About 50 seconds. VISION. Nothing on this slide is built except the inner ring (the job agent).
Say: The destination is full life coverage. The order is the point: job search first, because it is live and trusted; then the career around the job (first interview to offer, offer to day 90: notice, move, benefits, first paycheck); then the rest of life, added only as users ask for it.
Do not describe life features in the present tense. No dates.
Basis: the full-life vision with the job as the wedge, and our wedge-to-life review: viable as a vision and roadmap on conditions (two labels, staged rings gated by data, the job wedge as the moat, trust and channel limits named, life bundled into job plans rather than sold separately). It is not a description of today's product.
Not proven: that job-tool users want life help from their job tool. None was found either way in a bounded search (Oct 13)."""

