N9 = """About 50 seconds. VISION and roadmap. Gated by data, not dates.
Now: the job agent (live) plus the proposed core.
Career (ring 1), first interview to offer to day 90: offer comparison, notice and start date, relocation, first week, benefits deadlines, first paycheck, the next move. Triggered by job events Tsenta already sees.
Life (ring 2): life tasks users bring to the agent unprompted, if they do, added one at a time.
The rest of life (ring 3): one agent and one approval record. Bundled into the job plans with usage quotas as retention, mainly in the higher tiers, not unlimited on the entry plan and not sold as a separate life subscription; no life price is proposed (life use would be bundled into job tiers with usage quotas).
Gates (proposed tests): L1 classify inbound owned-channel messages and open Ring 2 only if non-career requests pass a set share (our channel research suggests 25% over 2 months as a starting threshold); L2 offer a career-stage checklist at the offer stage and compare 90-day retention with users without it; L3 a "help with your move" opt-in for accepted offers, measuring opt-in.
Reversible by design: each ring runs against a protected control group on today's job agent; if it fails, it closes and users keep the job agent and their record.
Channels: the life stages (rings 2 and 3) start on channels whose rules allow a broad assistant (app, iMessage, email) before WhatsApp, with fresh consent for each new purpose.
Not claimed: any life feature exists, any date, user demand, or that precedents prove it."""

N10 = """About 40 seconds. PROPOSED pilot with existing users. A test of the churn hypothesis, not a fix. Do not promise zero churn risk: trust, pricing and channel risks remain and are measured, not assumed away.
Tests (from our landscape test list): T4 proactive notes, at most one evidence-backed note a week; T5 interview-stage continuation; T6 re-entry check-in after a hire; T9 packaging control (search-window pass or pause, no agent changes). Plus a protected control group that stays on today's job agent.
Kill or narrow: if muted or regretted beats acted-on; if packaging alone moves retention as much as the agent; if MCP use is negligible, keep MCP as maintenance.
Why packaging is in: rivals price by search window, and a hire ends a search, so some churn may be success, not failure.
Measurement rule (runtime review synthesis): read retention among users who reach their goal (an interview, an offer or a hire) against the control group, with the guardrail that the offer rate is no worse than control. Never limit interviews or slow a search to improve retention."""

