NC = """About 45 seconds. ILLUSTRATIVE. Every number here is list-price arithmetic (vendor pricing pages read Oct 13, 2026) on assumed activity, per ACTIVE user per month. It is not Tsenta's usage, not a vendor quote, not a price recommendation and not a margin. Say the words "illustrative" and "list prices" whenever these numbers are shown.
Source: our scale-cost model (Oct 13), arithmetic checked by hand. The three profiles at 1,000 users on the own-core Cloud Run runtime: light (job wedge) about $1.16, normal (active job search) about $4.42, heavy (full-life scenario) about $19.03. Across own-core runtimes (Cloud Run, Workers with Durable Objects, Lambda, Lambda tenant isolation) and 100 to 10,000 users, heavy runs $18.88 to $21.43. These supersede earlier draft figures.
Assumptions per active user-month: light 30 proactive checks, 20 chat turns, 10 browser minutes; normal 120, 80, 60; heavy 720, 300, 300. 10 to 15 percent of checks escalate to an agent turn; chat turns routed 70 percent to Haiku 5.5 and 30 percent to Sonnet 5.5; 80 percent prompt-cache hits on shared prefixes.
Why it scales: the state layer is a fixed floor (two always-on Postgres compute units, $152.64 a month before the first user; not a verified provider-supported high-availability or failover setup at that price), the runtime scales to zero (between $0.00 and $0.75 per user-month across the own-core runtimes and two vendor runtimes, AgentCore and Claude Managed Agents; Vertex Agent Engine reaches about $2.13 and per-user hibernating sandboxes about $3.01), and model tokens are most of the bill. One always-on VM per user (Fly, 1 GB, Hermes's documented minimum) is $7.00 per user-month whether the user is active or not. Without routing and caching, the normal-profile model bill is about six times higher.
Excluded: engineering and fork maintenance, security assessments and penetration tests, compliance audits (SOC 2 or other), enterprise support plans, custom or committed tiers. The heavy profile is a vision scenario; there is no life price, and life features would be bundled into job tiers with usage quotas if they ever ship."""

